Only the first token, and an uninterrupted repetition of that token, receives
an opening response. Space-prefixed fragments are stronger, especially capitals;
ordinary unspaced words are weaker than unfamiliar fragments. Function words,
whitespace, digits and punctuation have their own coarse opening levels.
This deliberately does not memorize the exact activation of each opening word.
